# rule.always.catch-dreams-for-followups

> **every followup you do not do becomes a caught dream, and the route that found it keeps a symlink to it.**

first run SAFE/CLEAN (`rule.always.fix-forward-under-scouts-honor`): safe and clean → fix now, no dream. a spoken followup is a deletion; a dream keeps the cue, the reason deferred, the shape of the fix. shape: `term=artifact.dream._.choice._.md`.

```sh
rhx symlink --at "$route/dreams/v$date.$kind.$slug.md" \
            --to ".dream/v$date.$kind.$slug.md" \
            --mode relative --idem findsert
```

a deferral for DIRT owes a FULCRUM too (dream = work, fulcrum = decision).

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| you would say "i'll flag that for later" | that phrase IS the cue: two questions, then fix or catch |
| a rule you just wrote fires on your next action and you route around it | sharpest cue |
| a documented command fails or a readme is stale | catch it |
| the fix belongs to another repo | catch as a `reseed` dream |
| the fix is large | catch it with the shape of the fix |
| route finishes with empty `$route/dreams/` | suspicious |

shape: `# 🌙 dream: $what-is-owed` · kind · owner · caught $date, then `.the cue that fired` · `.the gap, precisely` · `.the shape of the fix` · `.why it is not done in this round`.

blocker: a followup mentioned and never caught · a dream for a safe+clean fix · no symlink at the route · a dream inside a route rather than `.dream/` · a dirt deferral with no fulcrum.
nitpick: no `.the shape of the fix`.
